# S-843 T-958: Variance annotation on type parameter — [let a@Covariant] is parsed and
# annotation_to_variance produces Variance::Covariant before any class-env check.
# The type alias has a lowercase body (the param itself) — no unit constructors are
# extracted, so the TypeDecl entry contributes nothing to the runtime dict.
# Absence of === warn asserts zero type warnings: annotation_to_variance handles
# "Covariant" cleanly without falling through to an unknown-annotation warning.
[
  Wrapper: [type [let a@Covariant] a]
  result: 42
]
=== out
Dict({"Wrapper": Dict({}), "result": Int(42)})
